{"schema":2,"commit":"22440a2406dd3763442e1d320dd531013e0a54eb","branch":"feature/notes-sync-issue-key-rules","base_sha":"fbf853d256530c373382fc3199a0b462b37d43de","message":"Publish notes through servers that require an issue key in every commit\n\nServers that police commit messages - e.g. a Bitbucket hook requiring a\nJira key - check every commit a push introduces, notes commits included.\ngit writes those with fixed messages (\"Notes added by 'git notes add'\",\n\"... by 'git commit --amend'\", \"Merged notes from ...\"), so the pre-push\nhook's notes push was rejected on every push and attribution never left\nthe developer's machine. The rejected chain kept growing, so even a\nwell-formed commit would have been refused alongside the old ones.\n\nThe pre-push hook now hands the push to a hidden `blamely sync-notes`,\nwhich never pushes the local notes history as-is. It works out which\nnotes this clone changed since it last agreed with the remote (target -\u003e\nblob maps from the merge base, so differently fanned-out trees compare\ncorrectly) and republishes them on top of the remote tip, ONE notes\ncommit per annotated commit: that commit's note is its only change, and\nits message is the annotated commit's own message, verbatim, followed by\n\"Notes added by 'git notes add'\" - the line Oobeya matches notes commits\non. Nothing about the message is checked or rewritten: the commit's\nmessage already passed the server's rule when the code was pushed.\n\nA note goes out together with its commit: only notes on commits the\nserver has (remote-tracking refs) or receives in this push (the hook's\nstdin) are published. Notes on local-only commits - WIP branches, the\noriginals git leaves notes on after amend/rebase, gc'd targets - wait in\none local pending commit on top. The commits are built with a single\nfast-import run (3000 stuck notes take about a second) and pushed by\ncommit id after a CAS update of refs/notes/blamely, so a note written by\na concurrent commit is never overwritten. Only a ref race is retried; a\nrule rejection is final and its reason is printed.\n\nThe fetch is hardened against the user's environment: it goes to the URL\nbeing pushed to (a read mirror as fetch URL would hand over a stale\ntip), with --refmap= (a configured +refs/notes/* refspec would otherwise\noverwrite local notes), --no-tags and --recurse-submodules=no; git runs\nwith LC_ALL=C because a translated git defeated every message match; on\ngit \u003c 2.29 the fetch falls back from --no-write-fetch-head and restores\nFETCH_HEAD by hand; commit messages are read with cat-file --batch so\nlog.showSignature cannot break the parse. The hook also syncs from bare\nrepositories and tells users not to push refs/notes/blamely by hand.\n\nOnly the CLI writes notes (the editor plugins just read them), so there\nis no cross-language parity impact.","totals":{"added_lines":1399,"ai_added_lines":1399,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":41,"ai_deleted_lines":0,"human_deleted_lines":41,"files":6,"models":{"claude-opus-5-5":1399}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":1399,"accepted_lines":1399}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":1399,"cli":0,"completion":0,"human":41},"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":1,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":1,"lines":[{"start":13,"end":13,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5-5","gen_type":"chat"}]},{"path":"README.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":1,"deleted_lines":1,"ai_added_lines":1,"human_deleted_lines":1,"lines":[{"start":91,"end":91,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5-5","gen_type":"chat"},{"start":91,"end":91,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"}]},{"path":"cmd/blamely/main.go","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":38,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":38,"lines":[{"start":132,"end":132,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5-5","gen_type":"chat"},{"start":861,"end":897,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool"